Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:15:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add requirements.txt extras and the generate_tpch
 workflow

The platform now runs workload code on one shared Python 3.10 environment
in Airflow and Jupyter. This repository declares its extras in
requirements.txt (duckdb==1.5.6), installed at each run, constrained by
the platform lock.

generate_tpch.py generates TPC-H data with DuckDB and checks one entity's
row count; workflows/generate_tpch.json runs it for all eight entities.
CI installs requirements.txt with the platform lock as constraint. The
README and AGENTS.md describe packages, the Jupyter kernel and command.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
